</section></score></mdiv></body>
<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Our God forbid that we should boast,</l><l>Save in the death of Christ, our Lord;</l><l>All the vain things that charm us most,</l><l>We’d sacrifice them to His blood.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>There from His head, His hands, His feet,</l><l>Sorrow and love flowed mingled down;</l><l>Did e’er such love and sorrow meet,</l><l>Or thorns compose so rich a crown?</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>His dying crimson, from His head</l><l>Spreads o’er His body on the tree;</l><l>To all the world then am I dead,</l><l>And all the world is dead to me.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Were the whole realm of nature ours,</l><l>That were an offering far too small;</l><l>Love that transcends our highest pow’rs,</l><l>Demands our heart, our life, our all.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
